  "warning": "Operator-only. Never shown to the reader and never shipped with reader materials.",
  "design": {
    "name": "two-session washout, single reader",
    "why": "A single reader cannot read both arms of one scenario back to back without the second read measuring carry-over. Each scenario is therefore seen exactly once per session, and the two session reads of the same scenario are separated by at least 48 hours of washout.",
    "session_gap_hours_min": 48,
    "session1": "scenario/arm pairs A; the reader sees each of the six scenarios once, one arm each.",
    "session2": "scenario/arm pairs B; the reader sees the other arm of every scenario.",
    "balance": "each session carries three baseline and three candidate arms",
    "order": "scenario order inside each session is seeded and independent of arm role",
    "reader_sees": "images/reader/session1/S<k>.png and images/reader/session2/S<k>.png, where k is the scenario's 1-based position in questions.json. No file, folder or sheet cell in the reader hand-out names an arm role."
  },
  "seed": "ac06-2026-11-06-washout",
  "seed_method": {
    "arm_draw": "per scenario: n = int(sha256(seed + ':' + scenario)[:8], 16). The session-1 ROLE is baseline when n is even and candidate when n is odd; the session-2 role is the opposite. The arm LETTERS are then relabelled so A is always the session-1 arm and B the session-2 arm, so a letter does not imply a role. Reference values: S1 0x8895ddd1 odd -> candidate first; S2 0x5c0425fd odd -> candidate first, flipped by the balance correction below to baseline first; S3 0xe82850b0 even -> baseline first; S4 0xdc5babf9 odd -> candidate first; S5 0x7ca6f8c4 even -> baseline first; S6 0xe162641d odd -> candidate first.",
    "balance_correction": "the raw draw put four candidates in session 1 (S1, S2, S4, S6) and two baselines (S3, S5). The session-1 role of the candidate scenario with the smallest hash value, S2-dev-tooling (sha256 prefix 5c0425fd), was flipped so session 1 holds three of each. This is the only edit to the raw draw and it is deterministic.",
    "session_order": "session 1 lists the six scenarios sorted by sha256(seed + ':order1:' + scenario); session 2 by sha256(seed + ':order2:' + scenario)."
  },
  "role_check": {
